dist/
build/
*.ipa
.DS_Store

# The generated Xcode project — and *only* that one.
#
# The leading slash matters. Written as a bare `ios/` this matched every
# directory called `ios` at any depth, which included `plugins/keepalive/ios`
# and `plugins/socket/ios` — the Swift source of both native plugins. They
# were never committed, so the Mac clone had two plugins whose implementation
# was entirely missing, and `cap add ios` failed trying to read a directory
# that does not exist there.
#
# Nothing local shows this: the files are on disk here either way. It only
# appears on a fresh clone.
/ios/
